    "body": "Three documents that were sitting untracked in the owner's checkout. They are moved into the repository so GitHub holds them; this is the owner-approved cleanup of 4 October.\n\n**Files**\n- `docs/research/retired-mechanisms-catalogue-2026-10-01.md`: a 1,350-line catalogue of retired, failed and negative results by family (learned retrieval, admission and quantization, language/compiler, geometry), each with its verdict. It was prepared on 2026-10-01 from `origin/main` `70d8a223` as reconnaissance for principal-investigator review.\n- `docs/research/external-literature-reconnaissance-2026-10.md`: alternatives to dot-product attention and their integer feasibility, VSA/HDC capacity arithmetic, E8, BitNet, and multiplier-free kernels.\n- `docs/adr/0000-template.md`: the ADR template. The numbered ADRs exist; the template did not.\n\n**Edits:** none beyond two repository-root links in the catalogue made relative to `docs/research/`. Both reports are dated snapshots; their claims keep their stated scope and are not current authority.\n\n**Checks:** claim-wording gate passed. I scanned for secrets and sealed-panel content (none). All relative links resolve.\n\n**Not committed:** the OpenCode/Kimi/agent-team leftovers (`.opencode/`, `.omo/`, `.agents/teamwork/`, `opencode.json*`, local edits) are archived to iCloud as `owner-checkout-leftovers-20261004` (md5 `634a980b…`).\n\nReferences #820\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
